      "title": "HTTP Mental Model and Request/Response Flow",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "HTTP Mental Model and Request/Response Flow",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What HTTP Is",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Stateless== **request/response** protocol; text-based in HTTP/1.1, binary in HTTP/2 and 3",
                "Client sends ==one request==, server returns ==one response==",
                "Server keeps **no memory** between requests"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Message Anatomy",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Request",
                "Response"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "First line",
                  "`GET /path?query HTTP/1.1`",
                  "`HTTP/1.1 200 OK`"
                ],
                [
                  "Then",
                  "headers",
                  "headers"
                ],
                [
                  "Separator",
                  "blank line",
                  "blank line"
                ],
                [
                  "Body",
                  "optional",
                  "optional"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Page Load Flow",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "DNS lookup",
                    "sub": "name to IP",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "TCP + TLS",
                    "sub": "handshake",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Request",
                    "sub": "client sends",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Response",
                    "sub": "server replies",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Parse HTML",
                    "sub": "browser",
                    "ink": "red"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Parsing HTML fires ==more requests==: **CSS**, **JS**, images"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Why Sessions Exist",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Server hands out an ID: `Set-Cookie: sid=abc123`",
                "Client sends it back on every request: `Cookie: sid=abc123`"
              ],
              "style": "number",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "HTTP forgets you after each response. The ==cookie== carries the **session ID** so the server can recognise you."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "HTTP Methods and Idempotency",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "HTTP Methods and Idempotency",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. The Methods",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Method",
                "Does"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`GET`",
                  "reads a resource, **no body**"
                ],
                [
                  "`POST`",
                  "creates or triggers an action"
                ],
                [
                  "`PUT`",
                  "replaces the whole resource"
                ],
                [
                  "`PATCH`",
                  "changes part of it"
                ],
                [
                  "`DELETE`",
                  "removes it"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Safe and Idempotent",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Methods",
                "Safe",
                "Idempotent"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "GET, HEAD, OPTIONS",
                  "{green:yes}",
                  "{green:yes}"
                ],
                [
                  "PUT, DELETE",
                  "{red:no}",
                  "{green:yes}"
                ],
                [
                  "POST, PATCH",
                  "{red:no}",
                  "{red:not guaranteed}"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. PUT vs PATCH, HEAD, OPTIONS",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==PUT== sends the **full representation** and overwrites it",
                "==PATCH== sends **only the changed fields**",
                "==OPTIONS== asks which methods and headers are allowed: CORS preflight",
                "==HEAD== returns a GET's headers with no body"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "curl -X PUT https://x.io/users/7 -d '{\"name\":\"Ann\",\"role\":\"admin\"}'",
                "curl -X PATCH https://x.io/users/7 -d '{\"role\":\"admin\"}'"
              ],
              "note": "same user, full body vs one field"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Mistake",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "GET for a state-changing action",
                "Prefetchers, crawlers and caches fire GET without user intent"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Safe means no state change; ==idempotent== means repeating gives the same end state. Never put a delete or purchase behind a **GET** link."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
